{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["<b>And the she-ass saw me and turned aside before me.</b> And along with this, behold, this happened to you: that the she-ass turned aside from before me three times — yet how did you not set your heart to this as well?" "<b>Unless she turned aside from before me.</b> You should have thought that perhaps she turned aside from before me, for you already knew that there is before El, blessed be He, some intercession on Israel's behalf." "<b>For now I would have slain even you, and spared her.</b> And the reason I said 'Wherefore have you struck your she-ass?' as though laying blame, is because indeed you have now shown that even had I been slaying you and sparing her — in a manner that would have made you recognize that this was no mere happenstance at all — even so, you would not have refrained from going, like one who delivers himself to death in order to transgress the will of his Maker. For there is no greater apostasy than this."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:40:47.221416474Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}